    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed 2 failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Missing APPROVAL_STATUSES export** (governance.test.js:152)\n- **Issue**: Test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `finetune/index.js`, but it was only available through the default export\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `finetune/index.js:362-365`\n\n### 2. **Toxicity metric scoring bug** (eval/index.test.js:48)\n- **Issue**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving references as the second parameter but treating them as banned terms. This caused safe outputs to be flagged as \"toxic\" when they matched the reference text\n- **Fix**: Updated `toxicityMetric` signature to accept `references` as the second parameter but ignore it, using `defaultBannedTerms` instead. This allows the function to work correctly when called by `runEvaluations` which passes both outputs and references\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests now pass across all 8 test files. All public exports remain intact and backward compatible.",
